{
  "id": "queue-kanji-order-stable",
  "title": "The new cards are served in draw order: a word's unit is not pulled forward over other new cards, and each rebuild after an answer is the tail of the build before (C-28c)",
  "covers": [
    "queue.kanji_order_stable"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "new_per_day is 5, so the backfill share is floor(5 / 2) = 2. Three single-kanji words were graduated two days ago with Easy (review state, not due), created in this order: 日 (card ...10), 家 (card ...20), 本 (card ...30). The new deckless word 日本語 (card ...40) was created before the kanji notes 日 (card ...50), 家 (card ...60), 本 (card ...70) and 語 (card ...80), all new and deckless. 日, 家 and 本 are backfill kanji (oldest word first); 語 is not.",
    "Step 0: the share step draws 日 and 家 (2 of 2) and stops at 本. The deckless turn draws the unit of 日本語: 日 is already taken, so the unit is [本, 語, 日本語] (5 new cards = the goal). The order is the draw order: 日, 家, 本, 語, 日本語. After 日 the word 日本語 requires the card just introduced, but its unit is not the next one, so it is NOT pulled ahead of 家 (QueueBuilder rule 5, 'N is never reordered'). until_stop is 5.",
    "Steps 1-2 answer 日 and 家 Easy. Step 3: both are today's backfill (their words were introduced on an earlier day), the share is used up, and the rebuild is the tail of step 0: 本, 語, 日本語. until_stop is 3.",
    "Step 4 answers 本 Easy. Step 5: 語, 日本語 (the open group: the last card introduced is a kanji the next unit's word requires). until_stop is 2."
  ],
  "clock_ms": 1795168800000,
